rence is withheld.","id":"codex/review/client-name-issue-url","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"redactedRecords still cleans record.repository and dedupKey (follow-ups.js:287), and the tracking repository is no longer copied (:293-294). follow-ups.test.js:348-349 asserts the '<redacted>' repository and that no 'tools' appears anywhere in the record.","id":"codex/review-own-repository-alias-client-leak","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"publication.js:170 still feeds followUpLines from redactedRecords. follow-ups.test.js:338-343 asserts that the PR Follow-ups section excludes local names and contains '<redacted> import breaks'.","id":"codex/review-privacy-pr","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"followUpsMarkdown still titles the view '# Follow-ups' with no feature ID (follow-ups.js:437). follow-ups.test.js:440 asserts this.","id":"codex/review-client-name-view","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"The redactor regex at follow-ups.js:249 is unchanged and redacts every absolute path. follow-ups.test.js:341 asserts '/srv' is absent from follow-ups.md and the PR summary.","id":"codex/review-single-segment-path-leak","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"followUpLines (follow-ups.js:461-462) adds the unavailable line and suppresses 'no follow-ups' when records are unavailable. follow-ups.test.js:464-467 asserts this.","id":"codex/review-unavailable-none","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"followUpsMarkdown (follow-ups.js:433-440) reports 'known ... incomplete' and 'None known'. follow-ups.test.js:468-471 asserts this.","id":"codex/review-unavailable-view-none","status":"resolved"}],"findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"redacted-issue-link-unusable","classStatement":"A public issue reference that cannot be followed to the filed issue replaces the tracking link.","criterion":"R7","evidence":"renderFollowUps passes featureHomeRepository(core) as host (follow-ups.js:449). featureHomeRepository (268-270) returns the alias whose path contains the feature home. issueReference (262) then