e, but only after convergence.","id":"claude-code/review-metrics-repair-receipt-r7","path":"repository/cli/test/metrics-repair.test.js","severity":"low"},{"blocking":false,"classId":"missing-local-receipt-affected-suite","classStatement":"A test suite exercising changed code has no local receipt on the candidate tree.","criterion":"gate:review","evidence":"Receipt 4 uses --test-skip-pattern='desktop reevaluation uses the staged measurement'. ciRequiredChecks include 'Desktop contract on Ubuntu 24.04' and 'Desktop contract on Ubuntu 22.04'.","failureScenario":"Two conditions are needed together: a defect limited to the staged desktop reevaluation case, and local receipt 4 skipping that case. The planned 'Desktop contract on Ubuntu' CI would then report a recoverable failure after convergence.","id":"claude-code/review-desktop-staged-receipt-r7","path":"repository/apps/desktop/test/metrics-view.test.js","severity":"low"}],"gate":"review","historyAssessment":{"affected":["codex/review/client-name-issue-url","codex/review-own-repository-alias-client-leak","codex/review-privacy-pr","codex/review-client-name-view","codex/review-single-segment-path-leak","codex/review-unavailable-none","codex/review-unavailable-view-none"],"carryForwardReason":"This round changed only the tracking handling in redactedRecords and the issueReference and featureHomeRepository helpers, plus their callers in publication.js, the mirrors, PROTOCOL.md and the R5/R7 tests. Four closures carry forward. codex/review-metrics-stale: workflow-projection.js:111/147 (WITHDRAWN) is unchanged. codex/review-unavailable-cli-none: current.js:31-32 checks unavailable before printing 'No follow-ups.'. claude-code/review-r1-present-reopen-untested: the deriveReviewRecords pass 2 reopen (follow-ups.js:124-130) and its R1 test are unchanged and pass in receipt 0 (line 23). claude-code/review-r7-decide-render-untested: follow-ups.test.js:432-435 still reads follow-ups.md right after decide, before render, and passes in receipt 0 (line 32)."},"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"The candidate keeps client names and local paths out of issue, PR and view text: redactedRecords drops raw URLs and withholds listed names (follow-ups.js:259-294), and tests use a gh stub. The dependency-scan gate is not implemented and #147 files are untouched. No merge was attempted. The remaining R7 defect is a requirements failure, not a mandate violation.","outcome":"PASS"},"outcome":"FAIL","summary":"Round 7 replaces the URL redaction with issueReference. Two things are fixed. First, the over-redaction: only followUpRedactions names decide whether a URL is withheld. Second, the mangled URL: no surface prints a term-redacted URL any more. The PR summary now shows #N for an issue in the PR's own repository, which GitHub autolinks in a PR body. A new medium regression on regression path follow-ups.js blocks. renderFollowUps passes featureHomeRepository(core) as the host. In the default layout (workspace.js:227 puts the feature home at <repository>/docs/issues/<branch>), every issue filed in that repository is shown in the committed follow-ups.md as a bare `#N`. GitHub does not autolink references in repository files, so that is not a tracking link, and AC7 asks for one. The R7 test misses this because its fixture keeps the feature home outside the repository (test line 449 still sees the URL). Low receipt gaps on metrics-repair and the skipped desktop staged case remain; the planned Ubuntu CI covers them. Withholding a client-named URL on another repository's surface is a defensible mandate trade-off."}]}